1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,355
Can AI make competitor research faster while leaving you with evidence

2
00:00:04,355 --> 00:00:08,710
you can actually check? For a small business, that is the

3
00:00:08,710 --> 00:00:13,065
useful question behind the latest connected research tools. Getting material into

4
00:00:13,065 --> 00:00:15,440
an AI workflow may become easier.

5
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:20,919
But access is only one part of dependable research. Three recent

6
00:00:20,919 --> 00:00:26,397
sources point toward a practical response: try a bounded pilot, and

7
00:00:26,397 --> 00:00:30,880
evaluate retrieval, source inspection, maintenance, and human control together.

8
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:37,763
Crayon says its announced Insights API makes competitor insights available to

9
00:00:37,763 --> 00:00:43,647
AI tools or developers. Alongside details such as titles, summaries, dates,

10
00:00:43,647 --> 00:00:49,530
and competitor tags, it says users can request underlying text and

11
00:00:49,530 --> 00:00:50,600
source links.

12
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:54,340
That matters because a researcher could inspect the material behind a

13
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:58,080
summary. But this is a commercial capability claim from the company

14
00:00:58,080 --> 00:00:58,760
selling it.

15
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:04,431
The evidence reviewed here does not establish accuracy, pricing, eligibility, geographic

16
00:01:04,431 --> 00:01:10,102
coverage, or how much implementation work a small business would face.

17
00:01:10,102 --> 00:01:15,773
Treat the announcement as a capability to investigate, with affordability and

18
00:01:15,773 --> 00:01:17,320
usefulness still open.

19
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:24,117
Nielsen Norman Group adds a constraint. In its study of expert

20
00:01:24,117 --> 00:01:29,914
Claude users, participants reportedly spent more effort engineering context libraries than

21
00:01:29,914 --> 00:01:35,711
crafting prompts. Files became stale or went missing. One participant’s task-list

22
00:01:35,711 --> 00:01:39,400
connection repeatedly expired and needed manual reconnection.

23
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:43,557
For research, that raises a practical question: will the right background

24
00:01:43,557 --> 00:01:47,714
material still be available and current next week? The supplied study

25
00:01:47,714 --> 00:01:50,360
text gives neither sample size nor geography.

26
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:55,098
These expert-user experiences identify problems worth testing; they do not tell

27
00:01:55,098 --> 00:01:59,837
us how often small businesses will encounter them, or how much

28
00:01:59,837 --> 00:02:01,560
time maintenance will take.

29
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:07,094
A different setting supplies another caution. TechCrunch reports that Anthropic said

30
00:02:07,094 --> 00:02:11,629
it turned off live internet access for its internal evaluations until

31
00:02:11,629 --> 00:02:16,163
it could confidently monitor and control its agents. That establishes a

32
00:02:16,163 --> 00:02:17,400
reported company disclosure.

33
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:22,629
It is not independent verification of the incidents, and it gives

34
00:02:22,629 --> 00:02:27,858
us no failure rate for deployed research products. Frontier-lab evaluations also

35
00:02:27,858 --> 00:02:33,087
differ substantially from a small firm’s research work. Still, the disclosure

36
00:02:33,087 --> 00:02:37,840
makes human oversight a relevant question when considering connected agents.

37
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:42,782
These sources address different settings; together, they are not a comparative

38
00:02:42,782 --> 00:02:43,680
tool test.

39
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:49,445
Our inference is to test the whole workflow over repeated runs.

40
00:02:49,445 --> 00:02:54,210
Choose one competitor question and a limited set of public sources.

41
00:02:54,210 --> 00:02:58,975
Check whether summaries match the underlying passages, whether links remain usable,

42
00:02:58,975 --> 00:03:02,440
and whether dates and competitor labels are correct.

43
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:07,476
Record verification time and connection repairs alongside any time saved. Establish

44
00:03:07,476 --> 00:03:12,511
actual access costs and setup effort before expanding. A source link

45
00:03:12,511 --> 00:03:17,547
helps you investigate an answer. It does not establish that the

46
00:03:17,547 --> 00:03:18,920
workflow stays usable.

47
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:23,735
Decide in advance what evidence would justify continuing, and what errors

48
00:03:23,735 --> 00:03:28,550
or maintenance burden would make you stop. Keep the final research

49
00:03:28,550 --> 00:03:33,365
judgment with a person. This is a proposed pilot, not a

50
00:03:33,365 --> 00:03:34,240
reported result.

51
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:40,850
The evidence leaves important gaps. We lack direct accounts from small-business

52
00:03:40,850 --> 00:03:46,460
users, unsuccessful deployments, and customers whose data is analyzed. These English-language

53
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:52,070
sources do not establish performance in non-English markets. They also support

54
00:03:52,070 --> 00:03:55,640
no conclusion about customer-data handling or consent.

55
00:03:55,640 --> 00:04:01,859
Customer-feedback, interview, and survey workflows therefore need separate assessment. The opportunity

56
00:04:01,859 --> 00:04:08,079
is easier access to research material. Whether that becomes affordable, dependable

57
00:04:08,079 --> 00:04:14,298
research depends on what your pilot reveals about checking sources, maintaining

58
00:04:14,298 --> 00:04:16,560
connections, and retaining control.

59
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:20,480
Codex assisted with drafting this script from the cited sources.
